# Code Comments Language

All inline comments, block comments, and JSDoc/TSDoc comments in source code **must be written in English** – regardless of the spoken language used in the conversation.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
// Gibt die aktive Version zurück
function getActiveVersion() { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
// Returns the currently active Node.js version
function getActiveVersion() { ... }
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
/**
 * Führt einen nvm-Befehl aus und gibt stdout zurück.
 */
async function runNvm(args: string[]): Promise<string> { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
/**
 * Executes an nvm command and returns stdout.
 */
async function runNvm(args: string[]): Promise<string> { ... }
```

This rule applies to all file types: `.ts`, `.html`, `.scss`, `.json`, `.sh`, etc.

User-facing UI text, documentation files (`.md`), and commit messages are **not** affected by this rule.
